    "case_id": "amb1-case01-product-scope",
    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 6 USER]\ne050\tNorthline emailed this morning.\ne051\tThey can live with their manual CSV process for another quarter, although their operations lead may move to a different role by then.\ne052\tThat reduces the urgency, but it also means we could lose the person who understands the problem best.\ne053\tOur smaller customers are not asking for reporting.\ne054\tThey are asking for fewer confusing states and faster support.\ne055\tI am less sure this is a broad product signal than I was yesterday, but more sure the discovery could be valuable.\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne056\tThe new email separates two clocks: delivery can wait, but access to a knowledgeable collaborator may not.\ne057\tThat supports a narrower move—capture the workflow and test the reusable concept now without beginning full implementation.\ne058\tIt also strengthens the case for protecting the smaller-customer and reliability commitments, since their demand is current and repeated.\ne059\tThe open question is whether your team can conduct discovery without it becoming an unofficial project through momentum alone.",
